2026-09-09 23:35:53,924 | INFO | hr_assistant.pipeline | Final answer: [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Welcome to the company! Here is an overview of our leave policy:\n\n### **Probation Period Notice for New Employees**\n* **Duration:** All new employees undergo a **3-month probation period** from their date of joining.\n* **Leave Eligibility during Probation:** During probation, you are **not eligible for paid leave**. However, you may take unpaid leave in case of emergencies, subject to approval from your manager.\n\n---\n\n### **Leave Policy (Post-Probation / Full-Time Employees)**\n* **Annual Paid Leave:** Full-time employees are entitled to **20 days of paid annual leave** per calendar year.\n  * **Advance Request:** Leave requests must be submitted through the HR portal at least **5 working days in advance**.\n  * **Carry Forward:** Up to **5 days** of unused annual leave can be carried forward to the next calendar year.\n* **Sick Leave:** Employees get **10 paid sick days** per year (separate from annual leave).\n  * **Medical Certificate:** Required if sick leave extends beyond **2 consecutive days**.\n\n---\n\n### **Holidays**\n* **Public Holidays:** The company observes **12 public holidays** each year (refer to the official calendar published by HR).\n* **Compensatory Leave:** Employees who work on an official public holiday are eligible for compensatory off.\n\nIf you have any questions or need assistance applying for leave through the HR portal, feel free to ask!', 'extras': {'signature': ''}}]
